they came with sunflowers and  chrysanthemums and notes of condolence  and carried them down to the entrance of  the sandringham estate a place the royal  family knows well  the queen came here for christmas and  the prince and princess of wales own a  house on the estate  and when they arrive to greet  well-wishers well it may have felt like  coming home  they looked at the flowers now  enveloping the front gate  then spoke to dozens of people who  journeyed to north norfolk to see them  the mood was neighborly and prince  william was willing to share  through the world yesterday was  challenging memories  [Music]  you kind of think to yourself i've  prepared for this but i'm not that  prepared he said comparing the  procession of the late queen's coffin to  westminster hall  to his experience at the funeral of his  mother princess diana 25 years ago  it was a startling expression of  openness but it seemed in keeping with  this event for there were other moments  of warmth and emotion  when a schoolgirl called elizabeth  presented the princess of wales with a  toy kate came up with another plan  and i went with her to put the flowers  on the pool  do you remember what she said to you  she said  and very very humble and you could say  she was emotional  that um  and i just said you know sorry for your  loss  but he says everybody's loss  you know there's more than one way to  say goodbye to the queen and a lot of  people here have had a chance to speak  directly and offer their condolences to  the prince and princess of wales but it  didn't go according to plan for one  couple they said they were approached by  catherine princess of wales and they  became completely tongue-tied they  couldn't get anything out they're  mortified  but i think they'll be okay  the sandringham estate is much like  balmoral a place of peace and some  privacy for the royal family but its  famous chapel makes an annual appearance  queen elizabeth came here to worship on  christmas day  and it won't be the same without her  to not see the queen at three o'clock on  christmas day will just be  whatever for my whole life that's what  i've seen and we've always sat down at  three to do that so it'd be very strange  open and relatable prince william has  revealed something of himself at  sandringham as the royal family  commemorates the past and plans for the  future  john sparks sky news at sandringer
 

